    "notes": "Series order: XY-V, XY-H, XZ-V, XZ-H, YZ-V, YZ-H (index = 2·cut + pol). Polar rings at −40/−30/−20/−10/0 dB, outer ring +5 dB. V traces are solid red, H traces dashed blue; dashed traces digitized with gaps (some angles missing). Deep nulls (XY-H near 170°, YZ-H near 350°) are approximate."
   }
  ],
  "calculators": [
   {
    "id": "match",
    "title": "Match at operating frequency",
    "description": "Looks up the digitized S11 graph and converts it to VSWR, return loss and mismatch loss.",
    "inputs": [
     "f_mhz",
     "t_c"
    ],
    "outputs": [
     {
      "id": "s11_db",
      "label": "S11 at f",
      "unit": "dB",
      "expr": "curve(\"s11_2450\", f_mhz)",
      "format": "fixed2",
      "description": "Digitized evaluation-board S11 (dB(S(1,1))) at the operating frequency."
     },
     {
      "id": "rl_db",
      "label": "Return loss",
      "unit": "dB",
      "expr": "-s11_db",
      "format": "fixed2",
      "description": null
     },
     {
      "id": "gamma_mag",
      "label": "|Γ| (reflection coefficient)",
      "unit": null,
      "expr": "10^(s11_db/20)",
      "format": "fixed3",
      "description": null
     },
     {
      "id": "vswr",
      "label": "VSWR",
      "unit": null,
      "expr": "(1 + gamma_mag)/(1 - gamma_mag)",
      "format": "fixed2",
      "description": "VSWR = (1+|Γ|)/(1−|Γ|)"
     },
     {
      "id": "mismatch_loss_db",
      "label": "Mismatch loss",
      "unit": "dB",
      "expr": "-10*log10(1 - gamma_mag^2)",
      "format": "fixed3",
      "description": "ML = −10·log10(1−|Γ|²): power reflected back to the transmitter."
     },
     {
      "id": "p_reflected_pct",
      "label": "Reflected power",
      "unit": "%",
      "expr": "100*gamma_mag^2",
      "format": "fixed2",
      "description": null
     },
     {
      "id": "mismatch_loss_ref_db",
      "label": "Mismatch loss at 2450 MHz (pattern frequency)",
      "unit": "dB",
      "expr": "-10*log10(1 - 10^(curve(\"s11_2450\", 2450)/10))",
      "format": "fixed3",
      "description": "Mismatch at the frequency where the radiation patterns were measured; used to estimate the extra loss when operating off 2450 MHz."
     },
     {
      "id": "excess_mismatch_db",
      "label": "Extra mismatch vs pattern frequency",
      "unit": "dB",
      "expr": "max(0, mismatch_loss_db - mismatch_loss_ref_db)",
      "format": "fixed3",
      "description": "Derived (not in datasheet): additional mismatch loss relative to the frequency of the pattern measurement. Gains below are reduced by this amount."
     },
     {
      "id": "vswr_graph",
      "label": "VSWR from VSWR graph (temperature)",
      "unit": null,
      "expr": "curve(\"vswr_2450\", f_mhz, clamp(t_c, 25, 125))",
      "format": "fixed2",
      "description": "Low-confidence read of the VSWR-vs-temperature graph; in-band only reliable at the 2400/2500 MHz markers."
     }
    ],
    "page": 2
   },
   {
    "id": "direction",
    "title": "Directional gain",
    "description": null,
    "inputs": [
     "cut",
     "pol",
     "angle_deg"
    ],
    "outputs": [
     {
      "id": "g_v_dbi",
      "label": "Vertical-pol gain toward direction",
      "unit": "dBi",
      "expr": "pattern(\"pat_2450\", 2*cut, angle_deg)",
      "format": "fixed2",
      "description": null
     },
     {
      "id": "g_h_dbi",
      "label": "Horizontal-pol gain toward direction",
      "unit": "dBi",
      "expr": "pattern(\"pat_2450\", 2*cut + 1, angle_deg)",
      "format": "fixed2",
      "description": null
     },
     {
      "id": "g_total_dbi",
      "label": "Total gain (V + H) toward direction",
      "unit": "dBi",
      "expr": "lin2db(db2lin(g_v_dbi) + db2lin(g_h_dbi))",
      "format": "fixed2",
      "description": "Power sum of both polarizations (derived)."
     },
     {
      "id": "g_dir_dbi",
      "label": "Gain toward direction (selected polarization)",
      "unit": "dBi",
      "expr": "pol == 0 ? g_v_dbi : (pol == 1 ? g_h_dbi : g_total_dbi)",
      "format": "fixed2",
      "description": null
     },
     {
      "id": "xpd_db",
      "label": "Cross-polar discrimination (V − H)",
      "unit": "dB",
      "expr": "g_v_dbi - g_h_dbi",
      "format": "fixed2",
      "description": null
     },
     {
      "id": "g_peak_dbi",
      "label": "Peak gain (any cut, total)",
      "unit": "dBi",
      "expr": "max(spec.peak_gain.typ, lin2db(db2lin(tindex(\"cut_summary\", \"idx\", 0, \"peak\")) + db2lin(tindex(\"cut_summary\", \"idx\", 1, \"peak\"))), lin2db(db2lin(tindex(\"cut_summary\", \"idx\", 2, \"peak\")) + db2lin(tindex(\"cut_summary\", \"idx\", 3, \"peak\"))), lin2db(db2lin(tindex(\"cut_summary\", \"idx\", 4, \"peak\")) + db2lin(tindex(\"cut_summary\", \"idx\", 5, \"peak\"))))",
      "format": "fixed2",
      "description": "Conservative upper bound: per cut, V-peak and H-peak power-summed (even if at different angles), and the datasheet peak gain; the largest is used for regulatory checks."
     }
    ],
    "page": 3
   },
   {
    "id": "link",
    "title": "EIRP and free-space link budget",
    "description": "Derived physics (Friis free-space model). For a polarization-matched link use the matching polarization; a total-gain link assumes the receiver captures both.",
    "inputs": [
     "p_tx_dbm",
     "loss_db",
     "rx_gain_dbi",
     "sens_dbm",
     "req_margin_db",
     "dist_m",
     "f_mhz"
    ],
    "outputs": [
     {
      "id": "p_ant_dbm",
      "label": "Power delivered to antenna port",
      "unit": "dBm",
      "expr": "p_tx_dbm - loss_db",
      "format": "fixed2",
      "description": "TX power minus cable/matching loss."
     },
     {
      "id": "eirp_dbm",
      "label": "EIRP toward chosen direction",
      "unit": "dBm",
      "expr": "p_ant_dbm + g_dir_dbi - excess_mismatch_db",
      "format": "fixed2",
      "description": "EIRP = P_TX − L_cable + G(θ) − extra mismatch (derived)."
     },
     {
      "id": "eirp_mw",
      "label": "EIRP",
      "unit": "mW",
      "expr": "1000*dbm2w(eirp_dbm)",
      "format": "fixed3",
      "description": null
     },
     {
      "id": "erp_dbm",
      "label": "ERP toward chosen direction",
      "unit": "dBm",
      "expr": "eirp_dbm - 2.15",
      "format": "fixed2",
      "description": "ERP = EIRP − 2.15 dB (relative to a half-wave dipole)."
     },
     {
      "id": "erp_mw",
      "label": "ERP",
      "unit": "mW",
      "expr": "1000*dbm2w(erp_dbm)",
      "format": "fixed3",
      "description": null
     },
     {
      "id": "eirp_max_dbm",
      "label": "Worst-case EIRP (peak gain)",
      "unit": "dBm",
      "expr": "p_ant_dbm + g_peak_dbi - excess_mismatch_db",
      "format": "fixed2",
      "description": "EIRP using the highest gain in any measured cut (or the datasheet peak gain if higher) – what a regulator would measure."
     },
     {
      "id": "erp_max_dbm",
      "label": "Worst-case ERP (peak gain)",
      "unit": "dBm",
      "expr": "eirp_max_dbm - 2.15",
      "format": "fixed2",
      "description": null
     },
     {
      "id": "erp_max_mw",
      "label": "Worst-case ERP",
      "unit": "mW",
      "expr": "1000*dbm2w(erp_max_dbm)",
      "format": "fixed3",
      "description": null
     },
     {
      "id": "fspl_db",
      "label": "Free-space path loss",
      "unit": "dB",
      "expr": "20*log10(dist_m/1000) + 20*log10(f_mhz) + 32.44",
      "format": "fixed2",
      "description": "FSPL = 20·log10(d_km) + 20·log10(f_MHz) + 32.44 (Friis)."
     },
     {
      "id": "prx_dbm",
      "label": "Received power",
      "unit": "dBm",
      "expr": "eirp_dbm - fspl_db + rx_gain_dbi",
      "format": "fixed2",
      "description": null
     },
     {
      "id": "link_margin_db",
      "label": "Link margin",
      "unit": "dB",
      "expr": "prx_dbm - sens_dbm",
      "format": "fixed2",
      "description": "Received power above receiver sensitivity."
     },
     {
      "id": "range_max_m",
      "label": "Max free-space range (with required margin)",
      "unit": "m",
      "expr": "1000*10^((eirp_dbm + rx_gain_dbi - sens_dbm - req_margin_db - 32.44 - 20*log10(f_mhz))/20)",
      "format": "fixed0",
      "description": "Distance where the margin equals the required fade margin, solving the FSPL formula for d. Real-world range (ground reflection, obstacles, body loss) is usually much shorter."
     },
     {
      "id": "eirp_headroom_db",
      "label": "Headroom to selected EIRP limit (worst case)",
      "unit": "dB",
      "expr": "eirp_limit_dbm - eirp_max_dbm",
      "format": "fixed2",
      "description": null
     },
     {
      "id": "p_tx_max_for_limit_dbm",
      "label": "Max TX power for selected EIRP limit",
      "unit": "dBm",
      "expr": "eirp_limit_dbm - g_peak_dbi + loss_db + excess_mismatch_db",
      "format": "fixed2",
      "description": null
     }
    ],
    "page": null
   }
  ],
  "checks": [
   {
    "id": "f_off_graph",
    "severity": "error",
    "when": "isNaN(s11_db)",
    "message": "Frequency is outside the 1–4 GHz range of the datasheet's S11 graph."
   },
   {
    "id": "f_out_of_band",
    "severity": "warning",
    "when": "not isNaN(s11_db) and not between(f_mhz, spec.freq_min.min, spec.freq_max.max)",
    "message": "Frequency is outside the specified 2400–2500 MHz band; patterns were only measured at 2450 MHz."
   },
   {
    "id": "vswr_high",
    "severity": "warning",
    "when": "vswr > 2",
    "message": "VSWR above 2:1 (return loss < 9.5 dB): retune the matching network."
   },
   {
    "id": "rl_below_spec",
    "severity": "info",
    "when": "rl_db < spec.return_loss.min and vswr <= 2",
    "message": "Return loss is below the 9.5 dB datasheet minimum at this frequency."
   },
   {
    "id": "temp_range",
    "severity": "error",
    "when": "t_c < spec.t_op_min.min or t_c > spec.t_op_max.max",
    "message": "Temperature outside the −40…+125 °C operating range."
   },
   {
    "id": "temp_graph",
    "severity": "info",
    "when": "t_c < 25 and t_c >= spec.t_op_min.min",
    "message": "VSWR graph only covers +25 °C and +125 °C; the +25 °C curve is used below 25 °C."
   },
   {
    "id": "power_over_max",
    "severity": "error",
    "when": "p_ant_dbm > 10*log10(spec.power_max.max*1000)",
    "message": "Power at the antenna exceeds the 2 W CW input power rating (33 dBm)."
   },
   {
    "id": "eirp_over_limit",
    "severity": "error",
    "when": "eirp_max_dbm > eirp_limit_dbm",
    "message": "Worst-case EIRP exceeds the selected regulatory limit."
   },
   {
    "id": "etsi_328",
    "severity": "warning",
    "when": "between(f_mhz, 2400, 2483.5) and eirp_max_dbm > 20",
    "message": "2400–2483.5 MHz in the EU: ETSI EN 300 328 limits wideband data transmission to 100 mW (20 dBm) EIRP."
   },
   {
    "id": "ism_band",
    "severity": "info",
    "when": "between(f_mhz, 2483.5, 2500)",
    "message": "2483.5–2500 MHz is inside the antenna's band but outside the 2.4 GHz ISM allocation."
   },
   {
    "id": "near_field",
    "severity": "info",
    "when": "dist_m < 0.25",
    "message": "Distance is within ~2λ of a 2.45 GHz antenna; the far-field FSPL formula is not valid."
   },
   {
    "id": "margin_negative",
    "severity": "error",
    "when": "link_margin_db < 0",
    "message": "Received power is below the receiver sensitivity at this distance – the link will not close even in free space."
   },
   {
    "id": "margin_low",
    "severity": "warning",
    "when": "link_margin_db >= 0 and link_margin_db < req_margin_db",
    "message": "Link margin is below the required fade margin; expect dropouts from fading, body loss and obstacles."
   }
  ],
  "notes": [
   "All RF data are for Johanson's evaluation board 2450AT18A100-EB1SMA with its matching circuit (1.0 pF series, 2.7 nH shunt, 3.9 nH series). On another PCB the matching values and topology will differ; leave pads for a pi network.",
   "Mount with the mark facing up; feed-line width must give 50 Ω (p.1).",
   "Pattern scale: rings at −40…0 dB in 10 dB steps, outer ring +5 dB; the XZ-V cut peak/average (≈0.7 / −0.5 dBi digitized) agree with the 0.5 / −0.5 dBi datasheet values, which confirms the dBi reading.",
   "The S11 and VSWR graphs on p.2 disagree in-band (e.g. 2.4 GHz: S11 −12.9 dB ⇒ VSWR 1.58 vs VSWR marker 1.386). Calculators use S11 for VSWR/mismatch; the VSWR graph is offered separately for the temperature trend.",
   "The 'extra mismatch' correction is a SheetFox estimate relative to 2450 MHz, where the patterns were measured; efficiency change with frequency is not given in the datasheet."
  ]
 },
 "userState": null
}
